to the city: and the next day he departed with Barnabas to Derbe.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„And when they had preached the gospel to that city, and had taught many, they returned again to Lystra, and to Iconium, and Antioch,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙœconfirming the souls of the disciples, and exhorting them to continue in the faith, and that we must through much tribulation enter into the kingdom of God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒAnd when they had ordained them elders in every church, and had prayed with fasting, they commended them to the Lord, on whom they believed.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙEAnd after they had passed throughout Pisidia, they came to Pamphylia.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJAnd when they had preached the word in Perga, they went down into Attalia:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzand thence sailed to Antioch, from whence they had been recommended to the grace of God for the work which they fulfilled.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ©And when they were come, and had gathered the church together, they rehearsed all that God had done with them, and how he had opened the door of faith unto the Gentiles.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ2And there they abode long time with the disciples.¦layout ªlast_verse